=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data source: web `useTranslation` only — AchievementBadge.tsx is a pure presentational
    leaf fed an `achievement: AchievementData` (+ `size`) prop by its parent (Lifetime Stats
    page / RecentlyUnlockedAchievements / AchievementUnlockedToast). Native binds the snapshot
    through the P1/S8 AchievementBadgeSource seam; NO HTTP in the view.
  - Derived values (verbatim): isNearComplete = !unlocked && progress>=0.8; pct =
    Math.round(progress*100); locked ring sweep = pct/100 (web <ProgressRing value={pct}
    max={100}/>). Reproduced + unit-tested incl. the .5-rounds-up and non-finite branches.
  - Composition (web rounded tile):
      • badge circle -> ZStack: when LOCKED, an inline progress ring (amber statusWarning when
        near-complete = web #eab308, else muted = web #6b7280) with the icon centered at 50%
        opacity + grayscale (web `opacity-50 grayscale`); when UNLOCKED, the full-colour icon.
      • name        -> semibold, centered; amber (statusWarning = web yellow-400) when unlocked,
        secondary otherwise.
      • description -> muted, centered (web text-muted).
      • status      -> unlocked: t('lifetime.unlocked', '✓ Unlocked'); locked: `{pct}%`
        (monospaced/tabular-nums, web tabular-nums).
      • tile        -> unlocked amber tint+border (web yellow-500/[0.08]+/30); locked faint
        neutral tint via textPrimary@0.04 + border (web white/[0.03]+/[0.06], theme-adaptive);
        near-complete pulse (web animate-pulse), suppressed under Reduce Motion.
      • size sm/md/lg -> ring 56/72/96, stroke 3/4/5, icon 20/30/36, gap 4/8/12, name 12/14/16
        (web sizeConfig verbatim).
  - States (ALL rendered; each has a #if DEBUG preview + a projection/model unit test):
      loading (skeleton tile) · empty (resolved w/o achievement → friendly trophy placeholder,
      never a blank box) · error (parent query failure → message + Retry, web QueryError peer) ·
      data (unlocked / near-complete / locked) · stale (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh) ·
      offline (cached achievement kept + offline chip).
  - i18n (P1/S10): the web key is preserved VERBATIM — lifetime.unlocked = "✓ Unlocked".
    Native chrome namespaced achievement.{live,stale,offline,staleA11y,offlineA11y,loadingA11y,
    empty,errorTitle,retry} + achievement.a11y.{unlockedStatus,progressStatus}. Every
    code-referenced key is declared in AchievementBadge.strings; NO English literals in native
    code (all via AchievementBadgeStrings + Text(verbatim:)). achievement name/description/icon
    are data (Text(verbatim:)), exactly as the web renders props (not translated).
  - Accessibility: the tile is one combined VoiceOver element (name, description, spoken status —
    "Unlocked" / "N percent complete"); the freshness chip + Retry are labelled buttons; icon is
    decorative (accessibilityHidden); Dynamic-Type system fonts; reduce-motion honored (pulse +
    TSSkeleton shimmer + TSFadeIn).
